@* Batch AQC-1 (design spec §2's versioning law, the house fail-loud law):
    the visible, honest error state a real AQC version mismatch renders --
    NEVER a silent degrade. Rendered by App.razor INSTEAD OF the ordinary
    Router the moment the startup check (AqcContract.Satisfies) fails; not
    itself a routed page (no @page directive -- App.razor swaps it in
    directly, so a mismatch is caught before any route even resolves). *@

<div data-testid="contract-mismatch" style="max-width:640px;margin:4rem auto;padding:2rem;font-family:sans-serif;text-align:center;">
    <h1>This build of Bible Atlas can't talk to its server</h1>
    <p>
        The server advertises Atlas Query Contract version
        <strong data-testid="contract-mismatch-advertised">@Advertised</strong>,
        but this client build was compiled against
        <strong data-testid="contract-mismatch-client">@ClientVersion</strong>.
    </p>
    <p>
        This is a deployment mismatch, not a data problem -- reloading will
        not fix it. Please contact whoever deployed this build.
    </p>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>The advertised range, rendered as "min-max" (e.g. "0.2.0-0.5.0").</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string Advertised { get; set; } = "";

    public string ClientVersion => AqcContract.ClientVersion;
}
